<!--
  FreeCAD reads this at startup and it decides the product identity the user sees.

  It previously carried an earlier working name, and pointed MaintainerUrl at a repository that is
  not ours. Meanwhile the window title, set separately in src/Gui, said
  "Redrob CAD". So the application presented two different names depending on where you looked, and
  offered a third party's URL as its maintainer.

  One name, and it is the product's: Redrob CAD. scripts/sweep-strings.py reads Application from
  this file, so this is the single place the name is decided and every swept string follows it.

  ExeName is not cosmetic. FreeCAD builds every user folder from it (settings, macros, add-ons,
  cache, the log file) and names its single-instance socket after it. Left as "FreeCAD", this
  application shared all of those with any FreeCAD on the same computer: each overwrote the other's
  settings, and a file opened from the desktop could land in the other program's window. FreeCAD
  skips the vendor in those paths, so ExeVendor only sets Qt's organization name.

  DesktopFileName must match the installed desktop entry (ai.redrob.cad.desktop): on Wayland it is
  the application id that joins a window to its launcher and icon.
-->
<Branding version="1.0">
  <Application>Redrob CAD</Application>
  <WindowTitle>Redrob CAD</WindowTitle>
  <ExeName>Redrob CAD</ExeName>
  <ExeVendor>Redrob</ExeVendor>
  <DesktopFileName>ai.redrob.cad</DesktopFileName>
  <MaintainerUrl>https://github.com/redrob-labs/redrob-cad</MaintainerUrl>
</Branding>
